      "title": "Career Development Center",
      "description": "Career Development Center - University of New Haven Skip to main content University of New Haven Main Search Visit Apply Admissions Visit Opportunities The campus visit is one of the most important parts of your college selection process. Undergraduate Programs See All Visit Opportunities Graduate Programs See All Visit Opportunities Getting Here Campus Locations and Maps Shuttles & Transportation Parking Events Events Athletics New Haven Chargers Close CLOSE University of New Haven Main Request Info Visit Apply Give Employers Parents & Families Veterans Work at UNewHaven Corporate Partners Directory myCharger Riyadh, Saudi Arabia Campus Academics Academics Academics at the University Academic Programs College of Arts and Sciences Pompea College of Business Henry C. Lee College of Criminal Justice and Forensic Sciences Tagliatela College of Engineering School of Health Sciences Interdisciplinary Collaborative Library Academic Calendar and Course Schedules See More Course Catalog Academic Centers and Institutes Student Success and Support Honors Societies Core Curriculum Study Abroad Verto Education Study Abroad Experience Student Life Student Life Student Life Overview New Student Orientation Get Involved! Living on Campus Dining Career Development Safety & Security Accessibility Health & Wellness Student Affairs & Dean of Students Campus Store See More Commencement Commuter Resources About About About the University Mission Statement and Core Values Accreditation Facts & Figures Awards & Affiliations University Leadership Board of Governors Offices & Departments Campus Locations & Maps State-of-the-Art Facilities The Elevation Center Strategic Plan See More Employment Info for Visitors, Parking & Shuttles Title IX and Equal Opportunity Admissions Admissions Office of Admissions Apply Request Information Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions International Students Online Programs Tuition & Financial Aid Net Price Calculator Pre-College and Summer Youth Programs Inclusion Inclusion Everyone Belongs at the University of New Haven The Myatt Center Accessibility Resources Center Graduate and International Student Life IDEA Council Military & Veteran Affairs Spiritual Life and Campus Ministry Title IX Alumni & Friends Alumni & Friends Our Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Involvement Alumni Benefits Magazine Alumni Association Contact Alumni Relations Support the University Research Research Research Overview Labs & Groups Faculty Research Student Fellowships & Research Summer Undergraduate Research Fellowships (SURF) Grants & Sponsored Programs Explore Explore Explore the University West Haven & Beyond News and Media Events Camps and Conferences Community Spotlights The Arts on Campus Digital Downloads Athletics Athletics Social Media Instagram Facebook Tik Tok LinkedIn X YouTube Close Menu Section Menu Student Life / Career Development Center Prospective Students Alumni Employers Main Page Internship Guidelines Recruit Employment Outcomes Staff Frequently Asked Questions for Parents Bergami Internship Close Career Development Center From help choosing the right major – or switching to a better fit – to internships and co-ops, résumé building, interview training, and job listings in your field, our goal is to connect you with the services and resources you need to map out the career you envision. Contact Us At the University of New Haven, we re-imagined what the concept of career development should look like and created an approach that is integrative instead of merely transactional. That means future career success is built right into your entire academic experience. It also means that everyone in the University is involved in Career Development, not just a few dedicated staff members. It really does take a village, in our opinion, to sow the seeds of a successful career — from faculty members who design career-focused curricula, to Resident Assistants who are intensely engaged in setting up career workshops and seminars, to the many campus events where career development is always a presence, to career fairs that are discipline and major specific. And that’s only a small sample of what you can expect. For undergraduates, graduate students, alumni, and employers, Career Development is more than an office at the University of New Haven. It’s a philosophy, incorporated in our values — it’s our culture. Current Students Log in to myCharger to view all Career Development resources. myCharger We are on Handshake! Activate your account on Handshake, build a career profile, and match with opportunities such as internships, jobs, and more. Take me to Handshake Prospective Students We’re with you every step of the way. Let’s get started on creating a plan for success. Choosing your major Internships Student employment Graduate school preparation Click Here to Learn More Alumni We know your career needs are ongoing. You know that we’re your partner for life. Career change Networking Graduate school preparation Job search Click Here to Learn More Employers You have an opening?  We have the people. Let’s connect you to the top candidates. Information sessions Guest speaking opportunities On-campus interviews Online job postings Click Here to Learn More Virtual Tour Launch CDC - Career Development Center See for Yourself Take a virtual of the Career Development Center in the Bartels Student Activity Center. Upcoming Events There are a variety of opportunities for you to learn more about our programs, what it is like to be a student here, and the scholarships, assistantships and financial aid that we offer. Whether you want to meet us on campus or online, we have something for you. See All Events A Nationally Respected University University of New Haven Again Recognized by The Princeton Review Among Best Universities in the Nation In the University's profile in The Princeton Review's \"The Best 390 Colleges\" guidebook, students lauded professors who are \"amazing and want to help in any way they can,\" and the University's \"refreshingly diverse campus.\" It is the ninth year in a row The Princeton Review has included the University in its annual ratings of the nation's top colleges and universities. From The Princeton Review. Used with permission. ©2024 TPR Education IP Holding, LLC. The Princeton Review is not affiliated with Princeton University. Read More University of New Haven 300 Boston Post Road West Haven, CT 06516 (203) 932-7000 (800) 342-5864 Admissions News and Media Campus Locations and Maps Public Safety Library Employment Give Faculty & Staff Directory Emergency Notifications Strategic Plan Information Technology Support myCharger Alumni Email Title IX Instagram Facebook Tik Tok LinkedIn X YouTube Send Us Feedback Online Privacy Statement Online Accessibility Equal Opportunity and Wrongful Conduct Reporting"
